# `ctx.required` trap when a durable queue's home first opens in a spawned task

Compiler: batch-51 macOS binary (predates the ctx lane's A2). Run from
`/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/avra-services` (branch `services`, tree unedited).

## It traps under `avra test`, not under `avra run`

As a standalone program (`./avra run <dir>`) **every variant I tried runs clean**: the home opens
inside `spawn s.run()` and sees `ctx db` (printed `sent 1 | depth 1`, and with a parked first tick
`sent 2 | depth 2`). The trap only shows up as a **spec case** run by `./avra test`.

## The schedule repro (this directory, `src/main.av`)

    ./avra test /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-tristan-projects-tristanMatthias-avra/cb67f90b-1c62-4c44-b1ee-a6de51b2c9d0/scratchpad/engine_repros/ctx_spawn_schedule

Output (warnings filtered out: two `type.alias_copy` warnings from std-relation's `db.av:1041` and `:1051`):

    avra: while running ctx under a spawned schedule /  / the home opened in the spawned run sees the context @ …/ctx_spawn_schedule/src/main.av:41 under schedule 0 — AVRA_SCHED_SEED=0 replays it
    avra: the context `db` is required, and nothing set it before it was read
    proofs: 0 of 0 programs owed, evaluated in 0 ms
    STOPPED — the case or program named above trapped, and everything after it never ran
    watch: peak 376 MB, status 1

`main.schedule_cron.av` is a copy of the same file. `main.parked.av` is an every-2s variant that
passed under `test`, but only because no tick fell due: its clock is the real wall, so under the
virtual clock the home never opened.

## Shrunk: no schedule needed (`../ctx_spawn_queue`)

    ./avra test /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-tristan-projects-tristanMatthias-avra/cb67f90b-1c62-4c44-b1ee-a6de51b2c9d0/scratchpad/engine_repros/ctx_spawn_queue

A queue declared in a fn that sets `ctx db`, handed to a spawned **free fn** that calls
`q.send(…)`. The first case (no park before the send) already traps the same way:

    avra: while running a durable home opened in a spawned task /  / before the task parks @ …/ctx_spawn_queue/src/main.av:41 under schedule 0 — AVRA_SCHED_SEED=0 replays it
    avra: the context `db` is required, and nothing set it before it was read
    STOPPED — the case or program named above trapped, and everything after it never ran

So none of the lane's three suspects is needed:
- **A spawn inside a method body?** No: the spawn is in a plain fn, and the spawned callee is a free fn.
use @std.queue.{queue, HomeError}
use @std.queue_store.durable.{db, stored}
use @std.queue_store.fault.{homed}
use @std.relation.{codec}
use @std.sqlite.{Db}
use @std.time.{ms, sleep}

@codec
type Beat = { n: int }

fn send_now(q: queue<Beat>) -> int {
    match q.send(Beat { n: 1 }) { .Ok(_) -> 1, .Err(_) -> 0 }
}

